module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.lambda_value_has_no_derived_type_in_v2_infer

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data lambda_value_has_no_derived_type_in_v2_infer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "lambda_value_has_no_derived_type_in_v2_infer" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a lambda -- an Arrow node standing as a VALUE, its formals and return minted as fresh type variables by function-value lowering -- has no derived type in v2.compiler.infer. infer_gather_fold_init sends an Arrow to infer_gather_fold_not_derived, so the lambda's facts are the counted infer_grounding_not_derived frontier, and any row that asks for the lambda's own type refuses there. HARM: until gunbc#13028 that row was the Loop row of every collection fold -- it read the step callable's type as the carrier and refused at the step Arrow, so no fold-bearing module could infer on the native route. #13028 STOPPED THE FOLD ROW FROM ASKING (a collection fold iterates its step's BODY: v2.compiler.infer infer_loop_iteration_fold_child_targets, selected by v2.compiler.fold_lowering fold_realized_member_role) rather than answering the question, so the gap stands for every other position a lambda value reaches: an argument to a higher-order parameter that is not a fold slot, a lambda bound by `let`, a lambda returned from a function, a record field holding one.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is not the fold row's defect and not the frame's. Under a fold, the step's formals ARE instantiated (the member from the domain, the carrier from init) and its body IS typed; what is missing is the lambda's own Arrow type assembled from those -- `fn(carrier, member) -> body` -- which no row builds, because typing an Arrow VALUE needs its formals' types (fresh variables, instantiated only where a frame supplies them) and its body's type together, and a lambda outside a fold has no frame to supply the formals at all. Elsewhere it is ordinary type inference over the fresh variables (unification), which v2 infer does not have.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- a counted frontier entry, refused where a row demands the type, never fabricated. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; the lambda's type is decidable from its formals and body once its variables are solved. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: v2 infer derives a lambda value's Arrow type from its formals' types and its body's type, with its fresh variables either instantiated by the consuming position's declared formal (a higher-order parameter's declared fn type, applied through the existing application-instantiation route) or refused as undetermined -- SUFFICIENT FOR a lambda passed to a declared `fn(A) -> B` parameter to be judged against that parameter, and for the fold row's body-not-callable read to remain the only fold-specific arm.",
    "RECEIPT, gunbc#13735: a lambda at an Arrow-typed record field stays at this frontier. `fn oar_mk() -> OarA { OarA { p: fn(n) { n > 0 } } }` with `p: fn(Int) -> Bool` is ACCEPTED carrying the counted `inhabitance_undecidable_argument_type_not_derived` obligation, where the named-fn counterpart is accepted AND decided by the Arrow arm of v2.std.inhabitance. It is not decided by the arm, and claiming so would be rung inflation. Claim: v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_optional_at_required_witness `oar_arrow_lambda_ok_is_accepted_at_the_counted_frontier_holds` (a permanent control: it reds when the lambda's type is derived and flips to the decided form, never deleted).",
    "CURRENT PER PATH, branch n7/callback-argument-frame (a0c17c753d, on main c22acb7681): AN APPLICATION ARGUMENT IS JUDGED. A lambda passed to a function-typed parameter has its fresh inputs instantiated from the parameter's declared domain at the call's instances, after the callee and every non-callback actual settle (v2.compiler.infer infer_callback_argument_frame), and is judged at that parameter by its signature AT THAT POSITION -- those inputs, authored inputs as written, and the elided return as the BODY's derived type, never the expected one -- through the Arrow arm of v2.std.inhabitance (v2.compiler.infer infer_callback_signature). Claims: v2.test.claim.compiler.callback_argument_formal -- `apply_int(f: fn(x) { need_int(n: x) })` accepted and decided; a callback returning Res<Bool> where fn(Int) -> Res<Int> is declared REFUSES application_argument_does_not_inhabit at `f`; both were red on d935a9d2f9. The lambda's OWN facts are not rewritten, so every other position named above -- a `let`-bound lambda, a returned lambda, a record field (oar_arrow_lambda_ok_is_accepted_at_the_counted_frontier_holds) -- keeps this frontier, and a generic formal whose return parameter only the callback could fix (U in `fn(T) -> Res<U>`) stays undecided rather than learning U. CLASS RUNG unchanged (mitigatable, the minimum across positions); the application-argument path is structurally guaranteed for a readable first-order formal.",
    "CLIMB (stern-cat-126): THE TYPE IS THE VALUE'S OWN FACT. The earliest unjustified boundary was the value's own settle row: every frame that instantiates a fresh input (an application argument, a record field, a fold step) put the instance where the BODY reads it, but the Arrow itself took product formation over its fresh atoms and stayed on the frontier, so each consumer re-assembled the type at its own position (infer_entries_with_callback_signatures, infer_entries_with_construct_callback_signatures, and the body re-read in infer_function_literal_return_instances) -- three leaves of one rule. v2.compiler.infer infer_function_value_facts now derives the type where the value settles: a fresh input is the instance of the frame it was entered under (InferGatherFoldAcc.frame_instances, the same List<TypeVariableInstance> its body's references were typed with), an authored input as written, an unwritten return the BODY's type; a variable no frame instantiated leaves it UNDETERMINED at NotDerivedSite FunctionValueSignatureUndetermined, never guessed. Every consumer reads the value's own facts; the consumer-position assembly is deleted, and the generic matcher gained its ARROW arm (infer_match_generic_arrow: inputs paired in each arrow's DECLARED order through infer_arrow_ordered_domain_types -- never the domain Conj's stored child order, and nothing learned when an order is unreadable -- then codomain, learning instances only, never refusing, since alias normalization does not descend into arrow parts), so a callable actual's type fixes its formal's parameters by the one matcher -- the call's InferredFacts.type_instances now carries a key callback's K, which no route recorded before -- and the one judgment still read at the position is the ARITY refutation (infer_callback_arity_refutation), a relation between two parameter counts rather than a typing of the value. Positions now typed: application argument, record field, fold step, and a let-bound or returned value whose inputs are authored. STILL AT THE FRONTIER: a value with an unannotated input and no consuming frame (`let f = fn(x) { x }`), which needs unification v2 infer does not have; CLASS RUNG unchanged (mitigatable, the minimum across positions). Claims: v2.test.claim.compiler.function_value_type (a lambda-key sort's key type derived and equal to the call's K instance; an Int key against a String order refusing application_argument_does_not_inhabit at `key`, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode function_typed_argument_mismatch_accepted; supplied-value claims at infer_function_value_signature).",
    "SORT_BY (stern-cat-126): the collection roster's template projection reads CallableOf as a signature Arrow and a row's AlgebraTypeVariable as a binder of the signature (v2.compiler.fold_lowering collection_roster_type_variable), so the sort_by row's SortKey is instantiated per call through the ordinary application route into InferredFacts.type_instances; and a structure-bounded carrier's generator is fixed by the inhabitance row its instance inhabits (v2.compiler.infer infer_instances_with_bound_generators), so the key callable is framed at the carrier's element. The PRODUCTION sort_by roster row is NOT added here: a roster primitive-call head that is not imported is UNBOUND (v2.compiler.resolve resolve_atom_unscoped_unbound never falls through to the std.primitives tier), so adding the row unbinds every caller that does not import collection_sort_by_shape -- 64 files at this head. FRONTIER: the row lands in the same change as the sort_by declared-import sweep (the NAMESPACE-XL sort_by wave), whose interim seed-oracle typing then dissolves.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_function_value_facts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_callback_arity_refutation", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_instances_with_bound_generators", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.fold_lowering", decl_name: "collection_roster_type_variable", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.infer", decl_name: "infer_loop_iteration_fold_child_targets", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.fold_lowering", decl_name: "fold_step_body_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.anonymous_binder", decl_name: "fresh_type_variable", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
